from their elders.", "Guidance for daily life. Customs helped organise the lives of community members. Their role went beyond clothing and ceremonies.", "A variety of practices. Customs differed across communities and local contexts. Each custom should be understood in its local context."], "text": "Two forms of law. Communities had written and unwritten laws. Both show that communities had their own legal systems. Unwritten law. This is known as adat, or customary law. This meaning applies to the legal context discussed here. An inherited tradition. Communities passed customs down through generations. Younger generations learnt from their elders. Guidance for daily life. Customs helped organise the lives of community members. Their role went beyond clothing and ceremonies. A variety of practices. Customs differed across communities and local contexts. Each custom should be understood in its local context."}